          "domain": "craft-and-structure",
          "skill": "text-structure-and-purpose",
          "passage": "The following text is adapted from Maxim Gorky's 1913 memoir \"My Childhood.\" The narrator, recalling his early years in his grandfather's house on the Volga, describes the evenings on which his grandmother told stories.\n\nOn winter evenings, when the wind off the river had driven everyone indoors, grandmother sat near the stove with her hands folded in her lap and began, without warning, to speak. Her stories were not announcements; they arrived as if she had been telling them all afternoon to herself and had simply forgotten that anyone else might be listening. As she spoke, her broad face softened and her hands rose to shape a horse, a forest, a bargeman on the Volga, so that the words and the small movements seemed to be parts of the same single thing. Watching her, I came to understand for the first time that a story was less a sequence of events than a shape a person made in a quiet room.",
          "question": "Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?",
