          "band": 3,
          "domain": "information-and-ideas",
          "skill": "inferences",
          "passage": "Augustin Holl, an archaeologist of West Africa, has spent decades reexamining how the region's early complex societies took shape. In southeastern Mauritania, his spatiometric analysis of stone-built funerary monuments revealed patterned territorial divisions consistent with an organized Late Neolithic pastoral society rooted in the Sahara itself. At sites associated with the early Ghana Empire, the archaeological record likewise documents a long, locally grounded sequence of agricultural and craft intensification preceding the emergence of statehood. Because both the structured pastoral landscape of the Sahara and the deep economic foundations of the Ghana polity appear to have developed in place, Holl's combined findings suggest that ______",
