          "passage": "Across the twentieth century, life expectancy at birth in the United States rose substantially for both sexes, but the size of the female-male gap did not move in a single direction. Drawing on vital-statistics records compiled at decade-scale intervals, epidemiologists have argued that the difference between female and male life expectancy followed a non-monotone trajectory over the century: it grew steadily through the middle decades and then contracted as the century closed. The data shown in the table support this characterization because _______",
