          "type": "multiple-choice",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "band": 3,
          "domain": "standard-english-conventions",
          "skill": "form-structure-and-sense",
          "passage": "Faith Ringgold, an artist and art historian affiliated with the University of California, San Diego, became known for her story quilts, narrative textiles that collapse the boundary between fine art and craft. Her 1991 work 'Tar Beach' demonstrated that a single quilted surface could layer autobiography, fantasy, ______ political testimony, anchoring her place in the tradition of Black feminist art.",
