          "domain": "standard-english-conventions",
          "skill": "boundaries",
          "passage": "Classical historian Mary Beard ______ argues in SPQR: A History of Ancient Rome (2015) that Roman citizenship was never a fixed birthright. Over time, the category was deliberately extended through grants to allies, freedmen, and provincials, transforming Rome into a continually expanding political community rather than a closed ethnic club.",
