          "domain": "standard-english-conventions",
          "skill": "form-structure-and-sense",
          "passage": "Edward Said, who taught comparative literature at Columbia University, argued in 'Culture and Imperialism' (1993) that the canonical European novels of the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries cannot be read apart from imperial history. According to Said, these novels embed the assumptions of overseas empire so deeply that ______ very form — the marriage plot, the bildungsroman, the realist panorama — quietly underwrites colonial rule.",
