          "band": 4,
          "domain": "standard-english-conventions",
          "skill": "boundaries",
          "passage": "In Don't Sleep, There Are Snakes (2008), linguist Daniel Everett describes decades of fieldwork among the Pirahã of the Amazon and reports that their language appears to lack recursion, a feature that universal grammar treats as inevitable in any human ______ Everett argues, the grammar of Pirahã seems to be tightly constrained by a cultural commitment to immediate experience.",
          "question": "Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?",
